    <l n="1">4. Summa personarum divisio examina-</l>
    <l n="2">tur.</l>
    <l n="3">5. Servus etiam ut res considerari pote-</l>
    <l n="4">rit.</l>
    <l n="5">6. Quo sensu summa dicatur divisio?</l>
    <l n="6">7. Adscriptitii, &amp; statu liberi qui sint?</l>
    <l n="7">8. Quid moribus sint homines proprii?</l>
    <l n="8">9. Utrum omnes servi dominum habe-</l>
    <l n="9">ant?</l>
    <l n="10" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">Definitio libertatis explicatur.</l>
    <l n="12" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="13">1. Explicatur servitus.</l>
    <l n="14">2. An servitus sit contra naturam?</l>
    <l n="15" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="16">1. Servi unde dicti, &amp; quomodo?</l>
    <l n="17">2. Quis modus vendendi servos?</l>
    <l n="18" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="19">1. Quot generum sint servi?</l>
    <l n="20">2. Jure Mosaico servos fuisse voluntarios.</l>
    <l n="21">3. Etiam antiquo jure Germanorum.</l>
    <l n="22">4. Jure Can. amitti libertatem propter</l>
    <l n="23">operas non</l>
    <l n="24">praestitas.</l>
    <l n="25" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="26">1. Servorum est differentia ratione sta-</l>
    <l n="27">tus.</l>
    <l n="28">2. Aliqua tamen servari videtur inter</l>
    <l n="29">publicos &amp; privatos.</l>
    <l n="30">3. Quot generum servi jure Mosaico?</l>
    <l n="31">4. Quid consuetudine generali obtineat?</l>
    <l n="32">5. Liberorum hominum conditio non est uniformis.</l>
    <l n="33" type="heading" level="1" caput="1" para="true">LIBR. I. TIT. 4.</l>
    <l n="34" type="heading" level="1" caput="1">De Ingenuis.</l>
    <l n="35" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Init.</l>
    <l n="36">1. Quis sit ingenuus?</l>
    <l n="37">2. Ex matre libera nascitur liber.</l>
    <l n="38">Calamitas parentum partui non obest.</l>
    <l n="39">Jure Hebraeorum quandoque materna</l>
    <l n="40">spectatur origo.</l>
    <l n="41">Quid moribus obtineat, explicatur.</l>
    <l n="42" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. I.</l>
    <l n="43">Quid sit, esse in servitute?</l>
    <l n="44">Jure Mosaico partus quandoque ven-</l>
    <l n="45">trem sequitur.</l>
    <l n="46" type="heading" level="1" caput="5" para="true">LIBR. I. TIT. 5.</l>
    <l n="47" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Libertinis.</l>
    <l n="48" type="heading" level="3" para="true">Init.</l>
    <l n="49" para="true">Libertini olim à libertis distincti.</l>
    <l n="50" para="true">Non omnis Manumissus conse-</l>
    <l n="51">quitur libertatem.</l>
    <l n="52">Unde dicta manumissio?</l>
    <l n="53">Omnes jure naturali sunt homines.</l>
    <l n="54" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. I.</l>
    <l n="55">Manumissio multiplex, ejusque effe-</l>
    <l n="56">ctus.</l>
    <l n="57">Modi quibus libertas competit, aut da-</l>
    <l n="58">tur, enumerantur.</l>
    <l n="59">Jure Mosaico quot modis servus liber-</l>
    <l n="60">tatem consequatur?</l>
    <l n="61">Moribus quid obtineat?</l>
    <l n="62">Quid jure Canonico?</l>
    <l n="63" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="64">Quotuplex status libertinorum?</l>
    <l n="65">Quid jure Mosaico obtineat?</l>
    <l n="66">Quid de consuetudine?</l>
    <l n="67">Quid jure Canonico?</l>
    <l n="68" type="heading" level="1" caput="6" para="true">LIBR. I. TIT. 6.</l>
    <l n="69">Qui, &amp; ex quibus causis manum. non licet.</l>
    <l n="70" type="heading" level="3" para="true">Init.</l>
    <l n="71" para="true">Non omnis qui manumittitur,</l>
    <l n="72">consequitur libertatem.</l>
    <l n="73" para="true">Qui manumittit in fraudem credito-</l>
    <l n="74">rum nihil agit.</l>
    <l n="75" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 1.</l>
  </main_text>
